{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QATKTsfC5HAPLe81eFDDGK","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_4/projects/trace-verdict-study/memory.md\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# trace-verdict-study Memory\\\\n\\\\n## MVP Round 1 结论（已作废）[2026-05-14]\\\\n\\\\nRound 1 结果全部无效，原因：\\\\n1. **VOTA match 泄漏**：assertion output 中 `match=True/False` 直接泄漏 verdict，99.2% accuracy 是 pattern matching 而非理解 trace\\\\n2. **Label 截断**：full_trace 28.4% 是因为 label 在序列末尾被 tokenizer 截断，模型根本没学到正确标签\\\\n\\\\n### 教训\\\\n- VOTA 输出中任何直接或间接暴露 pass/fail 的字段都是 data leakage——审查 trace format 时需要\\\\\\\"如果模型只看这一个字段能否猜到答案\\\\\\\"的测试\\\\n- 训练数据格式化必须保证 label 不被截断——应先预留 label token budget，再分配 trace 空间\\\\n- `[No trace available - execution failed]` 这类文本也是隐性泄漏（暗示 fail）\\\\n\\\\n## MVP Round 2 结果 [2026-05-15]\\\\n\\\\n### 三条件对比（数据已验证无泄漏）\\\\n- no_trace: 75.13% (CI: 72.8–77.5%), lift +3.6pp over majority baseline\\\\n- **VOTA: 95.63%** (Reviewer 修正，非之前的 99.16%), lift +20.5pp — 强 PASS\\\\n- full_trace: 28.4% — **genuine negative**（模型 1190/1190 全预测 fail，trace token 稀释分类梯度）\\\\n\\\\n**注意**：之前报告的 vota 99.16% 来自 v3 旧 eval（含 match 泄漏数据），实际 v4 accuracy 为 95.63%（来自 bootstrap_compare.json）。\\\\n\\\\n### full_trace 28.4% 根因（2026-05-15 最终诊断）\\\\n- **genuine negative，不是 bug**\\\\n- 模型 1190/1190 样本全部预测 fail\\\\n- 原因：full trace 的大量执行状态 token 稀释了分类梯度，模型无法从噪声中学到有效的判别信号\\\\n- chat template overhead（31 tokens）加剧了问题：100% pass 样本 label 在训练时被 TRL 右截断\\\\n- 对比 VOTA：assertion snapshots 信息密度高，即使 89.4% 被截断，剩余 10.6% 仍足以学到分类\\\\n\\\\n### 关键洞察\\\\n- VOTA 95.63% 是 genuine result（数据全量验证 match 字段出现 0 次），不是泄漏\\\\n- VOTA 的 assertion snapshots 包含 actual vs expected 值，提供高判别性信息\\\\n- **full trace 对 verdict 任务有害**——信息冗余 + 噪声稀释信号，支持 VOTA \\\\\\\"信息压缩\\\\\\\" 的核心论点\\\\n- 这个 negative result 实际上**强化了论文 story**：不是所有 trace 都有用，verdict-optimized 压缩是关键\\\\n\\\\n## 管线教训 [2026-05-14]\\\\n\\\\n### VOTA assertion snapshots 必须捕获 test 帧\\\\n- sys.settrace 的帧过滤不能只捕获 `<solution>` 文件——assert 语句在 `<test>` 文件中执行\\\\n\\\\n### exception 事件格式必须统一\\\\n- trace collector 与 VOTA 之间约定：`{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\": str, \\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\": str}`\\\\n\\\\n### prompt 必须包含 test code（控制变量）\\\\n- 所有条件的 prompt 都必须包含 test code，性能差异应严格归因于 execution trace 本身\\\\n\\\\n### TRL 版本注意\\\\n- TRL 1.1.0 已将 `max_seq_length` 重命名为 `max_length`\\\\n\\\\n## 环境信息 [2026-05-14]\\\\n- westd-11235: 2x RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell 94GB, CUDA 12.8\\\\n- 模型通过 ModelScope CDN 下载（HuggingFace 太慢 ~1.3MB/s）\\\\n- \\\\\\\"pass\\\\\\\"/\\\\\\\"fail\\\\\\\" 在 Qwen2.5-Coder tokenizer 中均为单 token (6385/18403)\\\\n- Qwen2.5-Coder chat template overhead: 31 tokens\\\\n\\\\n## 流程教训\\\\n- submit_training_job 必须用，不能用 nohup——否则无监控无回调\\\\n- Worker 汇报\\\\\\\"实验失败\\\\\\\"需要交叉验证（exit code + log），曾出现误报\\\\n- 提交前先检查是否已有同条件实验在跑，避免重复提交产生遗留\\\\n- [2026-05-15] submit_training_job 提交时 --gpu 参数必须与 gpu_ids 对应的物理 GPU 一致，否则 OOM 撞卡\\\\n- [2026-05-15] 数据格式化 token budget 必须扣除 chat template overhead，否则训练时 TRL 右截断会切掉 label\\\\n- [2026-05-15] 旧 eval_results.json 可能残留在 checkpoint 目录中，新 run 如果覆盖 checkpoint 但未覆盖 eval 文件，会读到旧指标——始终以最新 bootstrap_compare.json 为准\\\\n\\\\n## 文献定位 [2026-05-14]\\\\n- Wang et al. (EMNLP 2025): 原始 trace 对 SFT 帮助有限 → 支持 VOTA \\\\\\\"需要压缩\\\\\\\" 的动机\\\\n- APPT (TSE 2024): 最近 competitor，79.7% patch correctness accuracy，BERT 非 decoder，无 trace\\\\n- **文献空白**：无现有工作做 compressed execution trace + SFT for binary verdict\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 2762, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01TSrxCczp3tUC739GDQ9F4n","session_id":"c0d0aa71-4c26-4502-9f93-ba58e9ae5292","uuid":"ad784020-dfcc-49d8-92b4-0951eb983c4b","timestamp":"2026-05-15T02:01:33.585Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01W5idUHP3xyuGpE3uaK8LEh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012AJJAsFMrjTuoH9H5Aft3M","name":"mcp__agent-ml-research__read_project_file","input":{"project":"trace-verdict-study","file":"paper_framing.md","max_chars":0},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3715,"cache_read_input_tokens":18930,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3715,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":43,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01TSrxCczp3tUC739GDQ9F4n","session_id":"c0d0aa71-4c26-4502-9f93-ba58e9ae5292","uuid":"d7656c58-a3c9-4409-a050-f14a03585d2e"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012AJJAsFMrjTuoH9H5Aft3M","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_4/projects/trace-verdict-study/paper_framing.md\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# Paper Framing — trace-verdict-study\\\\n\\\\n## Target Venue\\\\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (ARR submission)\\\\n- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\\\\n- Deadline: ARR May 25, 2026 (10 days from today)\\\\n\\\\n## Core Insight\\\\n\\\\nTrace SFT effectiveness depends critically on **trace granularity matching task output entropy**: verdict tasks (1-bit output) benefit massively from compact, decision-relevant trace abstractions (VOTA: +20.5pp), while full execution traces cause model collapse (-46.6pp) due to gradient dilution. The \\\\\\\"right\\\\\\\" trace is not \\\\\\\"more trace\\\\\\\" — it's the minimal information sufficient to determine the verdict.\\\\n\\\\n## Core Claims (≤3)\\\\n\\\\n1. **VOTA dramatically improves verdict prediction**: Verdict-Optimized Trace Abstraction (assertion-point state snapshots) provides +20.5pp accuracy improvement over no-trace baseline for test outcome prediction, with 95% CI [+17.7, +23.4] excluding zero.\\\\n\\\\n2. **Full execution traces hurt verdict tasks** ⚠️ PROVISIONAL (pending v5): Dense, uncompressed execution traces cause model collapse (28.49% accuracy, 100% predicting \\\\\\\"fail\\\\\\\"). Root cause under investigation: D004 identified chat template label truncation; v5 retraining will determine if collapse persists after fix. If persists → gradient dilution hypothesis. If recovers → reframe as \\\\\\\"trace compression improves token efficiency.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n3. **Information granularity, not information presence, determines trace SFT value**: Through systematic ablation of VOTA components (actual/expected values, exception summaries, loop compression), we identify which trace elements carry verdict-relevant signal vs. noise, providing design principles for task-optimized trace representations.\\\\n\\\\n## Story Spine\\\\n\\\\n- **Problem**: Existing trace SFT studies (DCSH, TracePile) evaluate only generative tasks and find limited benefit. No prior work has tested trace SFT on code behavior verdict tasks (binary pass/fail), nor designed trace representations specifically for classification.\\\\n\\\\n- **Existing approaches & gaps**: DCSH (EMNLP Findings 2025) tested 5 trace formats on generation tasks, finding limited benefit. TracePile (NeurIPS 2025) scaled to 2.6M samples but only evaluated generation. TRACED (ICSE 2024) showed traces help encoder-based classification, but nobody has tested decoder SFT. All existing trace formats are designed for full execution simulation, not classification.\\\\n\\\\n- **Our framing**: We ask \\\\\\\"does trace granularity need to match task complexity?\\\\\\\" and demonstrate that verdict tasks — with O(1) output entropy — benefit from a fundamentally different trace design principle than generation tasks. VOTA captures only decision-relevant execution states (assertion snapshots, exception summaries) rather than full simulation.\\\\n\\\\n- **Headline result template**: \\\\\\\"On test verdict prediction, VOTA-SFT achieves 95.6% accuracy (+20.5pp over no-trace baseline), while full execution trace SFT collapses to 28.5% — demonstrating that trace design granularity, not presence, determines SFT effectiveness for classification.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n## Venue Fit Risks\\\\n\\\\n- EMNLP主会 vs SE: 论文核心贡献是对 trace SFT 的 task-dependent 效果的系统性实证发现 + 新 trace representation，属于 NLP for code 方向。投 EMNLP Code track 合适。\\\\n- 单任务风险: 目前只在 test verdict prediction 一个任务上验证。需要至少加一个 verdict task（patch correctness 或 bug detection）才够 EMNLP Main。Findings 可能只需当前结果 + ablation。\\\\n- Leakage concern: 如果 ablation 证明 VOTA 效果主要来自 actual==expected 字符串比对，claim 需要调整为 \\\\\\\"verdict tasks 需要的不是 trace reasoning 而是 decision-relevant data points\\\\\\\"——仍然 publishable 但 framing 不同。\\\\n\\\\n## Contingency Framing\\\\n\\\\n### Claim 1 contingency (based on plan_001 ablation outcome)\\\\n\\\\n**If ablation shows genuine behavioral understanding** (去 actual/expected 后仍有显著提升 >80%):\\\\n→ Full positive framing: \\\\\\\"VOTA teaches execution-grounded verdict reasoning\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n**If ablation shows primarily string matching** (去 actual/expected 后 accuracy 降到 ~75%):\\\\n→ Adjusted framing: \\\\\\\"For verdict tasks, the critical trace element is the assertion-point state — not behavioral reasoning but targeted state comparison. This is still a novel finding because: (a) no one knew this before testing, (b) it explains WHY full traces fail (too much irrelevant state), (c) it provides practical design principles.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n### Claim 2 contingency (based on v5 full_trace outcome)\\\\n\\\\n**If v5 full_trace still collapses** (~28%):\\\\n→ Original framing holds: \\\\\\\"Full traces hurt due to gradient dilution / information overload\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n**If v5 full_trace recovers but < VOTA** (e.g., 70-85%):\\\\n→ Reframe: \\\\\\\"Both trace types help verdict tasks, but compressed traces (VOTA) provide higher information density per token — VOTA achieves higher accuracy with 5-10× fewer trace tokens. The finding shifts from 'full traces hurt' to 'trace compression provides strictly better token efficiency for classification.'\\\\\\\"\\\\n→ Claim 2 becomes: \\\\\\\"Trace compression is not just cost-saving but accuracy-improving for verdict tasks\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n**If v5 full_trace recovers and ≈ VOTA** (>90%):\\\\n→ Reframe: \\\\\\\"Trace content matters more than format for verdict tasks — both dense and compressed traces unlock behavioral understanding. VOTA's value is primarily practical (5× fewer tokens, faster training/inference) not accuracy.\\\\\\\"\\\\n→ Weakest scenario for novelty. Strengthen with calibration analysis + second task.\\\\n\\\\n## Key Open Questions (Post-MVP)\\\\n\\\\n1. actual/expected ablation 结果如何？→ 决定 Claim 1 的强度\\\\n2. full_trace + label-only loss 能否修复 collapse？→ 加强 Claim 2 的解释\\\\n3. 能否在第二个 verdict task 上复现？→ 决定 generalization claim\\\\n4. 需要多模型验证吗？→ 时间允许就加 DeepSeek-Coder\\\\n\\\\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\\\\n\\\\n| Concern | Planned Response |\\\\n|---------|-----------------|\\\\n| \\\\\\\"VOTA 95.63% 可能是 trivial actual==expected 比对\\\\\\\" | ablation 实验直接回应（P0 优先级） |\\\\n| \\\\\\\"只在一个任务/数据集上测试\\\\\\\" | 加 patch correctness task 或 CRUXEval verdict variant |\\\\n| \\\\\\\"只用一个模型\\\\\\\" | 加 DeepSeek-Coder-6.7B 复现（DCSH 同模型） |\\\\n| \\\\\\\"full_trace collapse 可能是实现 bug\\\\\\\" | label-only loss ablation 验证是 gradient dilution 而非 bug |\\\\n| \\\\\\\"VOTA 只是 feature engineering 不是方法创新\\\\\\\" | 定位为 empirical contribution: 系统性发现 + design principles + task-spectrum analysis |\\\\n| \\\\\\\"与 DCSH 的关系不清\\\\\\\" | 明确：我们 complement DCSH（他们做 generation，我们做 classification） |\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 6030, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01TSrxCczp3tUC739GDQ9F4n","session_id":"c0d0aa71-4c26-4502-9f93-ba58e9ae5292","uuid":"6631450f-9122-4c3d-9054-0eb5b306ec2e","timestamp":"2026-05-15T02:01:37.207Z"}
